# Try the API from VS Code (install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each request).
# Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/Rag.Api

@api = http://localhost:5209

### Is the API running?
GET {{api}}/health

### Which AI is in use, and the limits
GET {{api}}/api/info

### 1. Use the sample CV (or upload your own: POST /api/sessions with a multipart "files" field)
# @name sample
POST {{api}}/api/sessions/sample

### 2. Search the session's documents
GET {{api}}/api/search?q=experience with cloud deployment&topK=3&sessionId={{sample.response.body.sessionId}}

### 3. Job match (can take up to a minute with local models)
POST {{api}}/api/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "{{sample.response.body.sessionId}}",
  "jobAd": "## What you'll need\n- 2+ years of C# and .NET\n- Building REST APIs with ASP.NET Core\n- SQL and relational database design\n- Experience with Kubernetes"
}

### Error example: no session (404)
GET {{api}}/api/search?q=sql&sessionId=made-up
